# The build context is deliberately narrow: everything is excluded and only the
# four trees the image needs are let back in, then the heavy directories inside
# them are excluded again -- by NAME, with the files bin/BUNDLE.txt actually
# lists re-included one by one.
#
# This is not micro-optimisation, and the exceptions are not decoration.
# `engines/tools/` is 208 MB in this checkout and 187 MB is evidence data.
# The bundle lists only exact allowlisted metadata files because setup-time
# selftests open them fail-closed. An over-eager exclusion here does not fail the
# build; it produces an image that dies in the `setup` stage on a rented box,
# which is the same shape as the bug that had a MiniMax root capture die on
# GGUF test data that was never bundled. `bin/selftest_container.py` rung C5
# therefore checks every BUNDLE.txt entry against these patterns.
*
!bin
!registry
!engines
!docs
docs/*
!docs/schema
engines/*
!engines/tools
!engines/patches-v2
engines/tools/dione-evidence/*
!engines/tools/dione-evidence/bf16-config.json
!engines/tools/dione-evidence/bf16-index.json
!engines/tools/dione-evidence/m2-layer45-unexpected-keys.json
engines/tools/newarch-stagea-evidence
engines/tools/glm53-stagea-evidence
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence
engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/*
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/fruit-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/glm53-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/fruit-fp8-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/glm53-fp8-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/drowzeys-exl3-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/wrld-exl3-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/dy325-exl3-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/dy30-exl3-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/dy342-exl3-layer78-unexpected-keys.json
!engines/tools/layer-outer-evidence/wrld-flash-exl3-k3-layer45-unexpected-keys.json
engines/tools/hidden-replay-evidence
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store

# Panels are measurement inputs, not evidence: the container-native root
# capture reads them FROM the image (the SSH-era --panel-dir upload does not
# exist there). C5g asserts every BUNDLE.txt file survives this ignore file.
!engines/panels/**
# The ssh target's PID 1 (container/Dockerfile, stage ssh).
!container/ssh-start.sh
